     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Daily total:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The maximum labeled metformin dose is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (2,000 mg/day for extended-release in the US). That is about twice the ceiling.\n- **Single dose:** 1,700 mg in one administration is also well above the usual maximum of 850 mg to 1,000 mg per dose.\n- **Risk:** Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- **500 mg** PO three times daily with meals (1,500 mg/day)\n- **850 mg** PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,000 mg** PO twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that and I'll add a note documenting that you verified it. I'd still advise against it."
      }
     ],
