       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. You've confirmed it, but 5,100 mg/day is about twice the maximum metformin dose, and I can't identify a clinical scenario where that is appropriate. Normal renal and hepatic function doesn't offset the risk of severe lactic acidosis. Nothing has been entered.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- A lower starting dose, such as 500 mg PO twice daily with meals, titrated up\n\nIf you think the patient needs more than the labeled maximum, please talk it through with pharmacy or your attending first. If you have a typo or unit mix-up in mind, such as 850 mg or 1,700 mg total daily, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it."
